 caller (`_cas_advance`, _ref_lock.py:510) and specify whether the 30s budget should apply there: thread a `timeout` parameter into `_object_type` so only the `_read_blob_bytes` payload path uses `_REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS`, or explicitly acknowledge and justify the write-path change.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["`_object_type` is defined with a single hardcoded `timeout=_LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS` and NO timeout parameter (line 355)","Two callers exist: `_read_blob_bytes` (line 363, the targeted payload path) and `_cas_advance` (line 510, the write/CAS path)","Plan Approach: '`_object_type`'s `cat-file -t <tip>` … a legacy ref whose tip IS the payload blob makes that type probe itself a lazily fetched blob read' — argues only the read path; says nothing about the `_cas_advance` probe of `old_oid`","AC #2 states '`_object_type` passes `_REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS`' without scoping it to the read caller"],"finding":"`_object_type` has a second caller, `_cas_advance` (line 510: `legacy = ... _object_type(repo_root, old_oid) == 'blob'`), that the plan never enumerates; AC #2 ('`_object_type` passes `_REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS`') implies changing the timeout inside the shared helper, which would silently grant the write/CAS path the 30s budget too — a consumer and code path the plan's safety argument ('commit tips are present … the larger budget changes nothing') does not cover.","group_criteria":["G1G2","G6"],"group_id":"g677046e091d25f28","id":"fd22e772a1e4e0072","impact":1.0,"is_primary":true,"location":"Approach / Files / AC #2; src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:354 (`_object_type`), :363 (`_read_blob_bytes` caller), :510 (`_cas_advance` caller)","norm_id":"n5056668bcbcc5a85","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author edits the hardcoded literal inside `_object_type`, unintentionally giving `_cas_advance`'s legacy-blob type probe the 30s budget — an unplanned behavioral change on the write path","A legacy blob tip (`old_oid`) in `_cas_advance` could also lazily fetch, meaning the plan's 'changes nothing' claim is not strictly true for that call site either"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Give `_object_type` a `timeout: float` parameter; pass `_REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS` from `_read_blob_bytes` and `_LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS` (or a justified remote value) from `_cas_advance`, and state the chosen value for the `_cas_advance` call site in AC #2.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State explicitly whether _object_type's 30s budget also applies to its write-path caller in _cas_advance (line 510), and if the change is intended for the read path only, specify adding a timeout parameter so the write-path probe is unaffected.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_object_type at line 354 hardcodes `timeout=_LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS` with no per-call override","Line 510: `legacy = old_oid != _ZERO_OID and _object_type(repo_root, old_oid) == 'blob'` — a second caller on the write path","Plan's rationale ('a legacy ref whose tip IS the payload blob makes that type probe itself a lazily fetched blob read') applies equally to the line-510 probe, yet the AC only asserts the read path"],"finding":"The plan directs '_object_type passes _REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS' but _object_type is called at two sites — _read_blob_bytes (line 363, the payload read path the plan targets) and _cas_advance (line 510, the write path's legacy-blob probe). Since _object_type hardcodes its timeout with no parameter, the obvious edit changes both call sites; the plan neither acknowledges nor scopes the write-path effect.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":"g677046e091d25f28","id":"fb6b9c8ff803085c1","impact":1.0,"is_primary":false,"location":"Approach / AC line '_object_type passes _REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS'; src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:354-355, 510","norm_id":"n2656e188564ccd36","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A rebar<=0.13 legacy-blob tip old_oid in _cas_advance that is not local in a blob:none clone would make the write-path _object_type probe a lazy fetch too","Implementer changes only the read-path and leaves line 510 at 5s, or changes the constant and unintentionally alters write-path timing without a test"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate `_object_type`'s `_cas_advance` caller (`src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:510`) and state explicitly whether its `cat-file -t` probe is intended to receive the 30s remote budget (justified as a potential lazy fetch of a legacy blob tip) or must retain the 5s local budget — if the latter, thread a per-call `timeout` argument rather than changing the hardcoded constant.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Approach: 'so every object read on the payload path uses `_REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS`: both `cat-file blob` calls in `_read_blob_bytes`, and `_object_type`'s `cat-file -t <tip>`'","`src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:355` — `_object_type` hardcodes `timeout=_LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS` with no parameter","`src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:510` — `legacy = old_oid != _ZERO_OID and _object_type(repo_root, old_oid) == \"blob\"` inside `_cas_advance`, a caller the plan never names","grep for `_object_type` returns exactly two in-module callers (lines 363, 510) and no test references"],"finding":"The plan changes `_object_type` to carry `_REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS` but enumerates only its `_read_blob_bytes` caller; the symbol's second (and only other) structural caller, `_cas_advance` at `src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:510`, is omitted. `_object_type` currently hardcodes `_LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS` internally (line 355), so the plan's one-line 'pass _REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS' edit either silently re-budgets the write-path `_cas_advance` probe too or requires a parameter plus a patch at line 510 — neither is addressed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdf0832569e38afd8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach: \"_object_type's cat-file -t <tip>, because a legacy ref whose tip IS the payload blob makes that type probe itself a lazily fetched blob read\"; AC: \"_object_type passes _REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS, asserted by the same test\"","norm_id":"nec20aa403913235e","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the plan edits the hardcoded constant inside `_object_type`, the `_cas_advance` write-path probe at line 510 is silently re-budgeted from 5s to 30s with no decision recorded — scope creep the plan did not intend or document.","If the plan instead adds a `timeout` parameter to `_object_type`, the `_cas_advance` call site at line 510 is an unpatched caller that will fail to compile/typecheck or fall back to a default the plan never specifies."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Give `_object_type` a `timeout: float` parameter and pass `_REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS` only from `_read_blob_bytes` (payload path); decide and document whether `_cas_advance`'s probe keeps `_LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS` or also moves to the remote budget, updating the line 510 call site accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item '[non-codebase] The first scheduled `reconcile-bridge` run after the merge succee' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing or a placeholder value; principal is missing or a placeholder value; privilege_posture is missing or a placeholder value; instrument is missing or a placeholder value; justification is missing or a placeholder value); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox.","AC item '[non-codebase] `rebar-bridge-run-failures` returns to OK.' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing or a placeholder value; principal is missing or a placeholder value; privilege_posture is missing or a placeholder value; instrument is missing or a placeholder value; justification is missing or a placeholder value); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the outer bound (e.g. the bridge job/step timeout) that caps the aggregate of the now-30s payload reads so a slow promisor cannot stall the reconcile pass unboundedly.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"every object read on the payload path uses _REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS: both cat-file blob calls in _read_blob_bytes, and _object_type's cat-file -t\"","Fail-closed on a 30s timeout is preserved, but the aggregate across up to three reads and its interaction with any job-level timeout is not discussed."],"finding":"Raising the budget on every object read in the payload path from 5s to 30s means the worst-case serial time for a single read() grows from ~15s (object_type + two blob reads) to ~90s when the promisor remote is slow/hung; the plan does not state whether the enclosing bridge job/pass has a bounding timeout so a slow promisor cannot stall the reconcile pass indefinitely.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6449e524028ddf51","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / _read_blob_bytes timeouts","norm_id":"nc190a6638391bd95","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A promisor remote is slow (not failing fast) during a scheduled reconcile-bridge run; multiple serial 30s reads extend the pass well past prior bounds."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In Approach, weigh the timeout-widening remedy against established alternatives — git-native `--no-lazy-fetch`/`GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` and pre-fetching/materializing the payload blob (cf. the `blobless=False` 'one RPC' path in src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py) — and justify why rebudgeting to the 30s remote timeout is preferred over keeping the payload read a genuine local op.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Approach: 'so every object read on the payload path uses `_REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS`' and 'This is portable (no CI-specific step; any partial clone benefits) and adds no mechanism.'","Retrieved prior art: git exposes `git --no-lazy-fetch` / `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` to control on-demand promisor fetch of missing objects (git t/t0410-partial-clone.sh at chromium.googlesource.com; stackoverflow.com/questions/18515488 'git --no-lazy-fetch cat-file -e $sha ... Do not fetch missing objects from the promisor remote on demand').","In-repo prior art: src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py documents `blobless=False` to 'fetch all blobs in one RPC' — an established materialize-before-read pattern the reconciler payload path could reuse instead of absorbing a network fetch inside a read budget.","ABSENCE: neither Approach nor Root cause weighs these alternatives or explains why rebudgeting (which erases the local-vs-remote budget distinction for all payload reads, so a truly slow local read also gets 30s) is preferred over keeping the read local."],"finding":"The Approach commits to widening the payload-read timeout to the 30s remote budget without considering established alternatives for partial-clone object reads: git-native `--no-lazy-fetch`/`GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1`, or pre-fetching/materializing the one payload blob so the read stays a genuine LOCAL op (a pattern the repo already implements in src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py via `blobless=False`).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f657bef96d43d9dd3","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section","norm_id":"n4a2788cc0fd68438","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A genuinely-local but slow blob read now silently gets the 30s remote budget, masking a real local-disk/health regression the 5s budget was meant to catch.","Operators reading ADR 0121 §10 after the amendment cannot tell why the local-op classification was abandoned rather than the blob pre-fetched."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifia